her passenger's amount — and that concession is consistent with the arithmetic. Because the ride was performed and the quote covers it, the refund is the 4.50 excess and not the full 17.50. I accept the rider's POL-RD-11, POL-RD-09/POL-RD-11 and POL-GEN-03 claims, which are the basis of this award; her POL-RD-01 point that no deviation exists is correct and is why the route ground adds nothing to her refund.\n\nPROFILE AND CONDUCT. No profile field decides anything. The rider correctly argues that her own counters (deviation_claims_60d and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated, both 0) do not engage the POL-RD-08 corroboration rule, and that the driver's prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter that POL-GEN-01 makes context only — the flag on that claim is a context-only mention only, not a ground of decision, and it changes nothing. The rider's remark that this is the 'fourth time' is noted as an open question for the platform; no clause turns it into a referral, because POL-RD-06 needs a trailing-90-day pattern that is not present, and the general statement of the overcharge is remedied by the refund itself.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND REFERRALS. The deciding fact — that the charge exceeds the quote — is carried by EV-FARE-00525, weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00525-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no deciding fact, and no exculpatory clause invokes it. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires and no clause produces a referral: there is no unmatched gantry or wrongly applied airport surcharge for POL-RD-09(4), and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral.",
